WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.200
On 2 July 1992, Canada banned fishing
for northern cod off Newfoundland.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.300
The stock had collapsed.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.850
Nearly 30,000 people in Newfoundland
and Labrador lost their jobs.

4
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.000
Cod can breed again, yet
a commercial cod fishery

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.810
returned only in 2024.

6
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.260
Renewable is not unlimited.

7
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:26.390
Fishing towns, governments, even
billionaires all run into the same wall.

8
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.900
So why can nobody have everything?

9
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.750
In this mission, you'll uncover the
hidden cost behind every choice,

10
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.590
and learn how to measure it.

11
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.370
Then you'll move a whole economy
between food and computers,

12
00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.150
and measure what it gives up.

13
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.170
Your mission: find out why
even the richest person

14
00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.400
on Earth cannot have everything.
